# What goes into the package: everything is left out, then named. A new file stays out unless it
# is listed here, so sources, source maps and node_modules cannot ship by accident. vsce applies
# every `!` line whatever follows it, so a folder cannot be named with exceptions: bundled/ is
# listed by kind of file, which also leaves out the __pycache__ folders that running the server
# writes there.
**
!package.json
!LICENSE.md
!README.md
!out/extension.js
!out/webview.js
!out/webview.css
!out/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt
!bundled/*.txt
!bundled/**/*.py
!bundled/**/*.pyi
!bundled/**/py.typed
!bundled/**/*.dist-info/**
